# review packet: internal correspondence about the manuscripts, not part of any release.
# It was tracked, and an audit found the author's home path in three of its files and the
# account handle in four more -- in a repository being prepared as a double-blind archive.
# Nothing outside it reads it and no paper cites it, so it stays local.
.review/

# Third-party rule files, kept locally so the provenance audit can run and NOT redistributed here.
# The ENVMICRO file is CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, which no GPL release can carry; the RetroSim and GLORYx
# files carry no licence text this repository holds. Each is obtainable from its own project, and
# scripts/typed_edit/curated_third_party.py reports which of them it found rather than assuming.
# BioTransformer's reaction database, and the bank that holds 611 of its templates verbatim. Its
# README requires explicit permission for redistribution and that permission has not been sought,
# so neither is shipped. grail_metabolism/resources/extended_smirks_released.txt is the bank this
# repository releases; scripts/build_released_bank.py rebuilds one from the other and prices the
# removal at zero references lost.
grail_metabolism/resources/extended_smirks.txt
grail_metabolism/resources/external/bt_database_metabolicReactions.json
grail_metabolism/resources/external/bt_database_ENVMICRO_metabolicReactions.json
grail_metabolism/resources/external/retrosim_templates_general.json
grail_metabolism/resources/external/gloryx_reactionrules.csv
# and the standardisation file, which is LGPL and so redistributable, but contributes no
# template the bank uses: an obligation with no scientific return.
grail_metabolism/resources/external/bt_database_standardizationReactions.json

# Session-tool state, not the project's. These directories are written by editor plugins and
# assistants working in this checkout and say nothing about the method or its results.
.idea/
.remember/
.superpowers/

